- 60% of projects have scope creep (untracked changes)
- Average scope creep = 15% extra work (uncompensated)
- Lost profit: $40k × 20 × 15% × 40% margin = $48k/year in margin loss

**3. Client churn due to unhappy delivery**
- Assume 50% of clients would renew (typical for service businesses)
- 20% of clients don't renew specifically because of delivery issues (late, unclear communication, scope confusion)
- Lost repeat revenue: $40k × 20 projects/year × 50% renewal rate × 20% churn = $80k/year

**Total annual cost of Delivery gap: $160k - $250k+**

For smaller business ($500k/year, 15 projects/year):
- Delayed revenue: ~$10-15k
- Scope creep: ~$15-20k
- **Total: $25-35k/year**

For larger business ($10M/year, 250+ projects/year):
- Delayed revenue: ~$200-300k
- Scope creep: ~$400-500k
- Churn: ~$500-600k
- **Total: $1.1M-$1.4M/year**

