## 4. GAP #3: RETENTION — Customers Disappearing, No Upsells, Silent Churn

### → The Gap (What's Wrong, Why It Matters)

**You have zero system for keeping customers or growing them.**

- After delivery, you never check in with the client. They use your product/service or don't. You don't know which.
- You have no idea which customers are unhappy until they're gone (or they complain on Twitter).
- You don't track renewal dates. Contracts expire. You scramble at the last minute (or miss the opportunity).
- Happy clients never get asked for referrals. You leave free revenue on the table.
- You have no process to upsell or cross-sell. Customers who want more help leave because you didn't ask.

**Why it matters:**
- Repeat revenue costs 5x less to acquire than new revenue. You're ignoring your cheapest growth lever.
- Customer acquisition cost for SMBs: $2-5k per customer. Retention costs: $200/customer/year. ROI on retention is 10x better.
- Churn is silent. If 15% of customers leave annually and you don't notice, you lose 15% of revenue every year while spending 100% of time on new customer acquisition.
- Happy customers are your best sales channel. They refer, they trust, they upgrade. Unhappy customers do the opposite.

---

