## 5. GAP #4: MARKETING — Wasted Spend, Bad Targeting, No Feedback Loop

### → The Gap (What's Wrong, Why It Matters)

**Your marketing is optimizing for the wrong thing.**

- You measure "leads generated" not "leads that close" or "revenue per channel"
- You don't know which channels produce good-quality leads vs. tire-kickers
- Sales never tells marketing which leads actually converted. Marketing keeps targeting the wrong audience.
- You copy, headlines, and offers don't resonate. You keep doing what "feels right" instead of what actually works.
- You spend on ads/content for topics nobody cares about. You ignore topics your audience searches for constantly.

**Why it matters:**
- Every wasted marketing dollar is money that doesn't go into your business. For a $3M business, 10% marketing budget = $300k/year. If half is wasted (common), that's $150k down the drain.
- Bad targeting attracts low-quality leads. Your sales team wastes time. Close rate tanks.
- Without feedback, you can't improve. You keep repeating the same mistakes annually.
- Your positioning is weak. Competitors with clearer positioning get better leads + higher conversion.

